00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:00.930
Oba
Yozo

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:02.220
Is anyone here?

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:04.180
Yes!
Oba
Yozo

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:11.520
Is this Oba's?

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:13.520
Yeah.

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:17.530
Are you one of those pushy salesmen? I don't want to buy anything!

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:19.950
No, I'm, er...

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:22.160
Horiki!

00:02:23.030 --> 00:02:24.620
It's Horiki, isn't it?

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:27.910
It's been a long time.
I'm happy you found this place.

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:31.670
I have something to tell you.

00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:33.340
Uh...

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:35.050
He's an old friend of mine.

00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:37.760
Ah, sorry about that!

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:39.090
It's okay.

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:43.300
What's with your hair?

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:45.350
Well, you know...

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:50.230
Dear, don't stand around in the doorway. Why don't you have him come in?

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:52.560
Oh, that's right, come in.

00:03:02.990 --> 00:03:04.620
You seem to be doing well.

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:05.990
We got married.

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:07.240
How many have you had now?

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:08.910
Don't ask me that.

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:11.250
How many years has it been since I last saw you?

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:14.000
I had a couple of things to take care of.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:15.340
A couple?

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:17.550
Probably nothing worth mentioning.

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:21.800
What's this?

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:27.930
I heard your comics sell pretty well.

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:31.390
Please get us some tea...
Actually, better make that sake and snacks.

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:32.520
Okay!

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:35.610
I don't have much time, forget the sake.

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:37.400
It's all right.

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:43.570
Are you past your anxieties?

00:03:43.570 --> 00:03:46.030
You used to wash your hands just about every time you said something, didn't you?

00:03:46.030 --> 00:03:49.450
Hey, did you come to drag up bad memories?

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:51.160
No.

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:56.750
I'm fine now.

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:02.130
I feel like I became a real human thanks to her.

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:07.350
She seems like a nice girl.

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:08.560
Yeah.

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:14.730
Her specialty is trust.

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:16.270
Yeah.

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:24.240
She even trusted someone like me.

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:41.760
Isn't society just a collection of individuals?

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:52.520
After she told me that, I realized that society really was just a collection of individuals,

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:54.020
and I was no longer scared.

00:05:02.030 --> 00:05:06.200
Society isn't that big of a deal.

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:12.410
Hey.

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:14.660
Oh, have you been drinking again?

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:15.960
Hey, are you a virgin?

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:24.260
How rude to ask a question like that all of a sudden!

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:27.970
I'll quit drinking...

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:31.310
if you'll marry me.

00:05:32.850 --> 00:05:35.230
Save me.

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:37.850
Save me.

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:38.810
I beg of you.

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:47.150
So you tainted an untouched virgin.

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:53.040
I was reborn after meeting her.

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:56.290
She's my Maria.

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:07.630
Let's get this one.

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:11.600
Let's rent it together,

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:13.600
and live here, just the two of us.

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:16.350
But... Should we really?

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:19.230
We'll manage to afford it somehow.

00:06:19.940 --> 00:06:21.980
Somehow?

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:24.860
All I have to do is draw comics that sell.

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:26.440
Please go downstairs.

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:29.860
You shouldn't come in here.

00:06:30.530 --> 00:06:31.280
But...

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:36.200
Believe in me.

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:41.330
Okay.

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:14.070
I'll do anything to protect Yoshiko.

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:18.120
She's the first person that made me want to live for someone besides myself!

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:22.420
Nice, nice!

00:07:22.420 --> 00:07:24.960
So you're finally in the mood.

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:27.130
Draw quickly.

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:30.470
Society wants to know everything about you!

00:07:30.470 --> 00:07:34.640
You can become the most popular clown in Japan!

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:36.760
This is your reward.

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:39.520
I've got the manuscript!

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:53.160
That's how it is.

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:59.410
When I'm not working, I occasionally take her to the cinema or to eat in Ginza.

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:02.910
This must be what people call happiness.

00:08:02.910 --> 00:08:04.210
But...

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:10.840
People who read your comics will eventually want more excitement.

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:17.680
You haven't read any of my works, have you?

00:08:18.390 --> 00:08:20.970
I'm a hardcore clown.

00:08:20.970 --> 00:08:22.520
Don't underestimate me.

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:27.190
It's all lies anyway.

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:28.690
I can draw anything.

00:08:29.150 --> 00:08:31.740
Maybe about half of it is true.

00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:36.200
Well, I don't care either way.

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:41.450
And after that?

00:08:42.700 --> 00:08:44.370
I'm asking what you're going to do after that.

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:46.830
You'll run out of material to sell quickly.

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:49.040
Well, that's definitely a problem.

00:08:49.460 --> 00:08:54.130
That's why I'm thinking about drawing something I really want to draw.

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:56.340
Like that?

00:08:57.010 --> 00:09:00.970
I haven't had much work lately, but I make enough to eat.

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:03.980
Excuse me.

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:08.730
Here it comes!

00:09:09.020 --> 00:09:11.690
It's been a while since we last drank together!

00:09:11.690 --> 00:09:12.980
Well...

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:14.740
What's the matter?

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:16.400
This isn't like you.

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:18.410
Uh...

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:21.910
Your boss is downstairs.

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:22.990
Huh?

00:09:22.990 --> 00:09:25.290
Was today the deadline?

00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:26.830
See, drinking sake right now would be...

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:28.120
What the hell are you saying!

00:09:28.120 --> 00:09:30.040
Tell him to wait a bit.

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:32.920
He'll get bored fast and go
home while we're drinking.

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:34.130
That'd be bad!

00:09:34.130 --> 00:09:35.340
This is...

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:37.260
It's okay, it's okay.

00:09:42.430 --> 00:09:47.520
I'm glad you came to visit me.

00:09:49.150 --> 00:09:50.270
What about our snacks?

00:09:50.270 --> 00:09:52.320
I'm cooking beans...

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:53.480
They'll be done soon.

00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:54.940
Nice!

00:09:58.410 --> 00:10:00.030
C'mon, drink!

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:01.620
Today's a good day!

00:10:17.220 --> 00:10:19.010
U-Uhm.

00:10:38.190 --> 00:10:40.820
By the way, what did you come here for?

00:10:41.530 --> 00:10:44.370
Oh right.

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:51.710
The day before yesterday,
I ran into that flounder guy...

00:10:52.670 --> 00:10:54.960
Sounds like your dad passed away.

00:10:57.590 --> 00:10:59.130
A month ago.

00:11:00.050 --> 00:11:01.640
Seems he had a peptic ulcer.

00:11:02.390 --> 00:11:06.890
I know you said you wouldn't come back to
Tsugaru until you had become a first-class artist,

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:09.850
and that you resented your father.

00:11:10.350 --> 00:11:16.230
But I think the least you can do is follow the moral principles and put up an incense stick for him.

00:11:23.530 --> 00:11:25.330
Screw moral principles!

00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:28.160
Screw...

00:11:31.160 --> 00:11:32.250
Yozo...

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:40.130
I strayed from moral principles long ago.

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:42.880
So what the hell are you talking about?

00:11:43.220 --> 00:11:46.600
Moral principles? What a laugh!

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:52.020
You just wanted to get
acknowledged by your father!

00:11:53.140 --> 00:11:55.520
He was just a politician.

00:11:56.650 --> 00:11:59.480
He's not in this world anymore.

00:12:03.530 --> 00:12:04.860
Yozo!

00:12:04.860 --> 00:12:05.370
Hey!

00:12:06.370 --> 00:12:07.580
Are you all right?

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:14.670
It's all the same to me.

00:12:14.670 --> 00:12:16.080
My father.

00:12:16.080 --> 00:12:17.250
Society.

00:12:17.250 --> 00:12:18.670
Even me.

00:12:19.710 --> 00:12:22.340
As long as I have her, I...

00:12:24.680 --> 00:12:25.800
Yoshiko!

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:29.890
Hold on!

00:12:29.890 --> 00:12:31.810
I'll get you some water.

00:13:12.310 --> 00:13:13.270
Yozo!

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:48.050
Even this place is hell.

00:13:48.680 --> 00:13:49.680
Here too?

00:13:50.470 --> 00:13:52.850
Are there worse hells than this?

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:55.230
I wonder.

00:13:56.680 --> 00:13:58.390
I don't know what to say.

00:13:58.730 --> 00:14:01.730
Bad timing, but I have to go now.

00:14:02.150 --> 00:14:03.020
Go?

00:14:03.610 --> 00:14:04.570
Wait!

00:14:04.570 --> 00:14:05.440
Hey!

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:07.780
Being alone with her now is...!

00:14:08.530 --> 00:14:10.870
I have to go to hell too.

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:12.910
To hell?

00:14:12.910 --> 00:14:14.040
Yeah.

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:15.290
I enlisted.

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:17.750
Enlisted?

00:14:18.580 --> 00:14:20.000
In the army?

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:21.750
We're deploying tonight.

00:14:21.750 --> 00:14:23.460
I have to get ready.

00:14:23.460 --> 00:14:24.300
Bye!

00:14:24.300 --> 00:14:25.840
Wait, Horiki!

00:14:25.840 --> 00:14:27.420
Don't go!

00:14:27.420 --> 00:14:28.300
Please don't go!

00:14:28.300 --> 00:14:29.680
Don't ask for the impossible.

00:14:30.010 --> 00:14:32.260
Aren't you an artist?

00:14:32.260 --> 00:14:34.600
Why are you going to war?

00:14:34.600 --> 00:14:36.930
The world is about to break.

00:14:36.930 --> 00:14:41.150
Maybe I feel it even stronger because I'm an artist.

00:14:44.610 --> 00:14:46.070
Yozo.

00:14:46.070 --> 00:14:49.030
When does a human cross the line?

00:14:49.610 --> 00:14:54.200
It's when he takes things from others because he's hungry. Then he's not a human anymore.

00:14:54.740 --> 00:14:57.750
I wonder if you crossed it when you took that woman's life.

00:15:00.370 --> 00:15:02.330
I didn't kill her!

00:15:02.630 --> 00:15:03.840
I didn't...

00:15:03.840 --> 00:15:04.630
Well, listen!

00:15:04.630 --> 00:15:05.550
I didn't...

00:15:05.880 --> 00:15:11.590
You certainly did, but it's not as bad as it might seem, since you respected her will.

00:15:11.590 --> 00:15:16.220
But from now on, spoiled kids can't be allowed to live.

00:15:16.220 --> 00:15:21.100
In the coming era, everyone will stop being human and turn into beasts.

00:15:22.230 --> 00:15:25.360
If that's happening, I'm heading straight for it.

00:15:27.070 --> 00:15:30.360
I'll kill people from all over the world.

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:37.240
Well, take care.

00:15:40.830 --> 00:15:42.580
Not like you can.

00:15:58.010 --> 00:15:59.180
Why?

00:16:02.060 --> 00:16:05.270
Why didn't you save me?

00:16:07.570 --> 00:16:10.780
Save, as if I...

00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:15.280
So I didn't really have a job.

00:16:17.120 --> 00:16:23.250
It was ridiculous of me to think that
something like my comics would sell.

00:16:23.790 --> 00:16:29.800
In order to get me a job from that guy, you...

00:16:30.920 --> 00:16:34.970
Everything was my fault.

00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:51.860
Yoshiko was supposed to be my goddess.

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:56.990
But once you start suspecting someone of something,

00:16:57.780 --> 00:17:04.370
that faint feeling capable of changing your idea about them rears its ugly head.

00:17:43.660 --> 00:17:47.870
I can't go back to normal, right?

00:17:49.460 --> 00:17:54.550
I lack something that a human should have.

00:18:08.730 --> 00:18:12.650
I'm... no longer human.

00:18:39.680 --> 00:18:42.180
No!

00:18:50.810 --> 00:18:56.610
We flushed his stomach, but treating the patient would be difficult here.

00:18:57.490 --> 00:19:01.240
Then we have no choice but to put him into a madhouse.

00:19:01.780 --> 00:19:04.080
How soon is he going to be discharged?

00:19:04.080 --> 00:19:07.250
It would be best to watch over him for three days.

00:19:07.250 --> 00:19:10.120
Can't we do it a bit sooner?

00:19:10.540 --> 00:19:13.000
Well, I don't think that would...

00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:16.920
If we leave him here, he'll just try to commit suicide again.

00:19:16.920 --> 00:19:20.510
Geez, all he does is cause trouble for others.

00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:25.310
It seems Yozo's dying is quite against your interests.

00:19:26.060 --> 00:19:28.810
Well, I get it.

00:19:29.230 --> 00:19:35.150
You're still getting Yozo's allowance from his family in Tsugaru, right?

00:19:36.110 --> 00:19:40.860
If only I didn't have to look after that trash...

00:19:40.860 --> 00:19:42.820
Who do you think you're calling trash?

00:19:44.570 --> 00:19:51.660
The Yozo we know is very honest and sensitive.

00:19:52.080 --> 00:19:54.710
If only he didn't drink...

00:19:55.670 --> 00:20:02.630
No, even when he did, he was like a god.

00:21:22.840 --> 00:21:24.720
I've been waiting for you.

00:21:25.470 --> 00:21:27.510
What would you like?

00:21:28.720 --> 00:21:30.350
I'm in pain.

00:21:31.470 --> 00:21:34.930
Give me something that will put me at ease.

00:21:36.140 --> 00:21:37.100
Very well...

00:21:52.910 --> 00:21:56.660
Oh, there you are.

00:22:01.460 --> 00:22:05.170
We'll always be together from now on.

00:23:25.040 --> 00:23:30.050
